@host = http://localhost:3000

### A clean order: billing invoices it, email thanks the customer,
### analytics counts it. One publish, three independent consumers.
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ord-1", "customer": "a@example.com", "total": 100 }

### Retries with backoff: this customer fails three deliveries, then succeeds.
### Watch the WARN lines in the dev server output.
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ord-2", "customer": "flaky@example.com", "total": 50 }

### Two rejections for two reasons: billing throws reject() on a negative
### total, and email's zod schema refuses the same payload. Neither retries.
POST {{host}}/api/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ord-3", "customer": "c@example.com", "total": -5 }

### A different channel under the same prefix. Only the wildcard consumer
### (orders.#) sees it — billing and email do not.
POST {{host}}/api/orders/cancel
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "ord-1" }

### The second bus: fire-and-forget, so publish() resolves before delivery.
POST {{host}}/api/presence
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "u-42" }

### Everything the consumers have done so far.
GET {{host}}/api/state
